<SiteLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Fran Legacy website privacy policy.">
  <section class="legal-hero"><p class="section-kicker light">Legal</p><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p>Last updated August 20, 2026</p></section>
  <article class="legal-copy">
    <h2>Information we collect</h2><p>When you contact Fran Legacy, we may receive the information you provide, including your name, email address, telephone number, business details, property information, and documents related to a potential transaction.</p>
    <h2>How we use information</h2><p>We use submitted information to respond to inquiries, evaluate potential transactions, provide requested services, maintain business records, improve our website, and comply with legal obligations.</p>
    <h2>Sharing and retention</h2><p>We do not sell personal information. We may share information with professional advisers, service providers, lenders, title companies, contractors, or transaction partners when reasonably necessary and subject to appropriate confidentiality expectations. We retain information for as long as needed for the purposes described here.</p>
    <h2>Security</h2><p>We take reasonable steps to protect information, but no internet transmission or storage method is completely secure. Do not send sensitive financial credentials through an unencrypted email.</p>
    <h2>Your choices</h2><p>You may request access, correction, or deletion of personal information by emailing <a href="mailto:tfrancisco@franlegacy.com">tfrancisco@franlegacy.com</a>. Certain records may be retained where required by law or legitimate business needs.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2><p>Fran Legacy, 4208 Six Forks Rd, Suite 1000, Raleigh, NC 27609 · 877-450-1550.</p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
